.TITLE "mount"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Attaches a filesystem found on a device to the main filesystem tree. It allows you to __access storage__ from external drives, partitions, or network locations.

.DIV "TLDR"
**mount**
Displays a list of all currently mounted filesystems and their locations.
> 

**mount device destination**
Attaches a specific device or partition to a directory in the filesystem.
> __device__ source (e.g., /dev/sdb1) | __destination__ target directory

**mount -t type device destination**
Mounts a filesystem while explicitly specifying its type (e.g., ext4, ntfs).
> __-t__ type flag | __type__ filesystem type | __device__ source | __destination__ target

**mount -a**
Mounts all filesystems listed in the configuration file (/etc/fstab).
> __-a__ all flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
You typically need __root privileges__ to mount devices. After you are finished with an external drive, always use __umount__ to safely detach it and prevent data corruption.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:umount** **linux:lsblk** **linux:fdisk**

documentation: __https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man8/mount.8.html__
